  "plain": "President John F. Kennedy is said to have done something odd in June 1963: ordering the printing of silver certificates, a kind of paper money backed by silver. The lawyer Dan Sheehan brings it up, mentioning the film director Oliver Stone, and admits he has never quite figured out why Kennedy did it, telling it among other hints that Kennedy was acting on secrets in his last months."
